The shared `tracker-sync` hook shipped in the plugin's own `playbooks/_scripts/` resolves from the
core discovery root and runs `booping-tracker sync` against the artifact. Under the default `cli`
driver the tracker performs no write and exits 0, so the edge completes and the report names the
hook. A successful hook's own stdout is captured by `playbook-transition` and never relayed, so the
tracker's receipt does not appear here — only `script tracker-sync: ok` does.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  tracker:
    driver: cli
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-tracker/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-tracker
title: Tracker
summary: Tracker-hook fixture for playbook-transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-tracker/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  only: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: noted
            when: the run moves on
            hooks: ["script tracker-sync"]
      noted: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-tracker/only/prompt.md --
---
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- fixtures/cwd/run/.keep --
-- cmd --
booping playbook-transition fx-tracker intaking --workdir run
booping playbook-transition fx-tracker noted --workdir run
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
created index.md
not-started → intaking
frontmatter: status=intaking
intaking → noted
frontmatter: status=noted
script tracker-sync: ok
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/run/index.md --
---
status: noted
---
